      "text": "Truth is not always easy to define, even when we believe we have it clear. What we consider true depends, to a large extent, on the information and perspective we have available. Recognizing the limits of our own knowledge is, perhaps, the first step toward a more honest understanding of the world. Doubt, well understood, is not weakness but method.",
